00:11:06,668 --> 00:11:09,939
input extension to keep the input file type.

268
00:11:10,195 --> 00:11:12,665
Then we create an encoder

269
00:11:13,242 --> 00:11:15,567
and that simply depends on which format

270
00:11:15,567 --> 00:11:18,020
we're targeting because that Bun API has

271
00:11:18,197 --> 00:11:20,185
different encoders for different image

272
00:11:20,297 --> 00:11:20,618
types.

273
00:11:21,243 --> 00:11:23,907
So here we simply get a little helper object

274
00:11:23,907 --> 00:11:24,163
back

275
00:11:24,773 --> 00:11:26,940
that simply describes which kind of encoder

276
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:30,214
we want and what the quality will be. And in

277
00:11:30,246 --> 00:11:32,429
case of PNG, we're actually converting a

278
00:11:32,493 --> 00:11:34,981
quality to a compression level because PNG

279
00:11:34,981 --> 00:11:37,373
doesn't have the notion of an image quality,

280
00:11:37,469 --> 00:11:39,010
it just has compression level.

281
00:11:39,555 --> 00:11:41,016
So we have a little helper function that

282
00:11:41,064 --> 00:11:44,130
converts a quality between 1 and 100 to a

283
00:11:44,130 --> 00:11:46,826
compression level between 0 and 9. That is

284
00:11:46,938 --> 00:11:47,869
what PNGs want.

285
00:11:49,264 --> 00:11:52,278
And once we have that encoder, we can use it

286
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:52,502
for

287
00:11:53,031 --> 00:11:54,858
encoding down here. Now before we do that,

288
00:11:55,436 --> 00:11:57,487
we compute the output path, which is simply

289
00:11:57,503 --> 00:11:59,780
the path where the optimized image should be

290
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:00,325
stored.

291
00:12:01,351 --> 00:12:03,258
Got a little helper function for that too,

292
00:12:03,771 --> 00:12:05,887
where we construct the output path by

293
00:12:05,999 --> 00:12:06,464
creating

294
00:12:07,314 --> 00:12:09,334
a fitting file name that has the right file

295
00:12:09,382 --> 00:12:12,908
extension and is then stored in an output

296
00:12:12,908 --> 00:12:15,361
path that is defined with help of the output

297
00:12:15,457 --> 00:12:18,984
dir or the out_dir flag, or if not set, it

298
00:12:19,064 --> 00:12:20,733
is by default stored stored in

299
00:12:21,471 --> 00:12:24,891
an optimized folder next to the input file.

300
00:12:25,662 --> 00:12:27,492
That is what we do here. We construct the

301
00:12:27,589 --> 00:12:30,206
path where the actual optimized images

302
00:12:30,318 --> 00:12:31,169
should be stored.

303
00:12:31,747 --> 00:12:34,027
Now we have a dry run option that can be set

304
00:12:34,092 --> 00:12:37,769
with --dry-run, which would actually not

305
00:12:37,769 --> 00:12:40,001
convert the images and instead just output

306
00:12:40,177 --> 00:12:42,104
what would happen if we would run the

307
00:12:42,104 --> 00:12:44,850
command without dry run being set. That can

308
00:12:44,850 --> 00:12:47,321
be nice for previewing what will happen.

309
00:12:47,898 --> 00:12:50,353
So in that case, we continue, we skip the

310
00:12:50,369 --> 00:12:51,540
rest of this loop here,

311
00:12:52,133 --> 00:12:54,235
and we just write which file we would be

312
00:12:54,235 --> 00:12:54,844
processing.

313
00:12:55,582 --> 00:12:58,310
If we have not set try_run, we do the actual

314
00:12:58,406 --> 00:12:59,400
processing down there,

315
00:12:59,994 --> 00:13:02,432
and we optimize image after image with help

316
00:13:02,432 --> 00:13:04,951
of the optimize_one function. optimize_one

317
00:13:05,063 --> 00:13:07,999
gets our encoder as input and also gets the

318
00:13:08,095 --> 00:13:09,587
output and the input

319
00:13:10,181 --> 00:13:13,052
absolute paths as inputs. So optimizeOne is

320
00:13:13,164 --> 00:13:16,178
the main function that actually uses that

321
00:13:16,210 --> 00:13:17,508
Bun Image API.

322
00:13:18,053 --> 00:13:20,137
And what we're doing in here is we're

323
00:13:20,201 --> 00:13:22,365
getting our file, we're reading it with the

324
00:13:22,462 --> 00:13:25,716
bun.file method, another feature built into

325
00:13:25,748 --> 00:13:28,441
the Bun API. So coming right from the Bun

326
00:13:28,633 --> 00:13:31,727
runtime, file is there to read files very

327
00:13:31,759 --> 00:13:32,321
efficiently.

328
00:13:33,202 --> 00:13:33,298
We

329
00:13:33,827 --> 00:13:36,809
get the size of that file here, the number

330
00:13:36,809 --> 00:13:37,883
of bytes in there.

331
00:13:38,973 --> 00:13:41,442
And then this here, that's the Bun Image

332
00:13:41,442 --> 00:13:43,830
API. So another feature coming from the Bun

333
00:13:44,407 --> 00:13:45,401
runtime in the end.

334
00:13:45,930 --> 00:13:48,559
On a file that we read with bun.file and

335
00:13:48,816 --> 00:13:50,948
only on files that we read with bun.file,

336
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:54,026
not on files that we read with any Node.js

337
00:13:54,218 --> 00:13:57,055
API, for example, but on files that we read

338
00:13:57,087 --> 00:13:59,700
with bun.file, we can call image because

339
00:13:59,796 --> 00:14:01,752
file and image are both coming from Bun.

340
00:14:02,377 --> 00:14:05,872
And image in the end gives us a handle to an

341
00:14:06,048 --> 00:14:09,318
object that has various optimization and

342
00:14:09,414 --> 00:14:12,270
conversion methods. For example, a resize

343
00:14:12,303 --> 00:14:14,485
method for changing the file size in case

344
00:14:14,485 --> 00:14:16,894
the user did set different width and height

345
00:14:16,894 --> 00:14:17,250
values.

346
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,570
If not, we're not doing any resizing, of

347
00:14:19,604 --> 00:14:19,941
course.

348
00:14:22,176 --> 00:14:25,952
And then in the end, we also use the JPEG,

349
00:14:25,968 --> 00:14:29,646
the PNG, WebP, or AWITH methods on that

350
00:14:29,663 --> 00:14:31,655
image handle, again, which is coming from

351
00:14:32,154 --> 00:14:33,979
Bun depending on which encoder was picked.

352
00:14:34,189 --> 00:14:36,354
So if we have the JPEG encoder, we call the

353
00:14:36,354 --> 00:14:38,114
JPEG method on that Bun Image API.

354
00:14:38,722 --> 00:14:41,561
For the PNG encoder, we call PNG and so on.

355
00:14:41,914 --> 00:14:43,422
So that is what then actually

356
00:14:43,999 --> 00:14:47,303
encodes the optimized image as a JPEG, as a

357
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:51,634
PNG and so on after resizing it. And we set

358
00:14:51,634 --> 00:14:53,351
the quality level of the encoding here,

359
00:14:53,399 --> 00:14:55,532
which of course also affects the file size.

360
00:14:55,965 --> 00:14:58,436
And then in the end on that encoded image,

361
00:14:58,452 --> 00:15:01,467
we call write, which is another Bun feature,

362
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:04,290
the write method, which is there to write

363
00:15:04,290 --> 00:15:07,482
something to a file and we write the image

364
00:15:07,674 --> 00:15:10,287
in the end into that output path. That is

365
00:15:10,383 --> 00:15:12,307
what actually creates and stores the

366
00:15:12,387 --> 00:15:13,124
optimized image.

367
00:15:14,326 --> 00:15:16,795
And that is what optimize1 does here. And we

368
00:15:16,811 --> 00:15:19,440
do that image after image. We keep track of

369
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,524
all the images we processed so that we know

370
00:15:21,604 --> 00:15:23,448
when to leave that loop once we processed

371
00:15:23,528 --> 00:15:25,948
all images. And we also keep track of the

372
00:15:26,028 --> 00:15:28,481
bytes we read in and the bytes we wrote out

373
00:15:28,673 --> 00:15:31,126
to see by how much we optimized the images.

374
00:15:31,543 --> 00:15:33,979
We also have verbose logging. So you can add

375
00:15:33,979 --> 00:15:37,650
a --verbose option to log more details and

376
00:15:37,650 --> 00:15:40,040
if that is turned on, we do, for example,

377
00:15:40,056 --> 00:15:42,622
calculate how much we actually shrank the

378
00:15:42,622 --> 00:15:45,412
images and we write that information to the

379
00:15:45,412 --> 00:15:46,262
log too.

380
00:15:46,936 --> 00:15:49,069
And that is essentially it. That is the

381
00:15:49,101 --> 00:15:52,212
entire program. We are processing images.

382
00:15:52,565 --> 00:15:54,730
And the main takeaway is of course that

383
00:15:54,795 --> 00:15:57,056
we're doing this with a mixture of Node.js

384
00:15:57,056 --> 00:16:00,151
APIs, but then most importantly also by

385
00:16:00,183 --> 00:16:03,712
using certain Bun APIs like the File API,

386
00:16:03,792 --> 00:16:04,706
the Image API,

387
00:16:05,235 --> 00:16:07,400
and that you can build a program like this

388
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:10,259
therefore without any extra dependencies.

389
00:16:10,532 --> 00:16:13,729
It's just the Bun runtime, nothing else, no

390
00:16:13,826 --> 00:16:16,557
third-party dependencies, just a Bun program

391
00:16:16,718 --> 00:16:17,762
executed with Bun.

392
00:16:18,485 --> 00:16:20,365
And I'm not just using the Bun runtime here,

393
00:16:21,056 --> 00:16:22,743
and I also used it for setting up the

394
00:16:22,743 --> 00:16:25,185
package.json file and installing this one

395
00:16:25,474 --> 00:16:27,691
type dependency, but instead we're also

396
00:16:27,707 --> 00:16:30,181
using the test runner capabilities because

397
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:32,639
in there, and again, you found it attached,

398
00:16:33,089 --> 00:16:35,033
you'll find a bunch of test files where we

399
00:16:35,033 --> 00:16:37,525
got little testing functions that test the

400
00:16:37,525 --> 00:16:41,012
various aspects of this program to make sure

401
00:16:41,061 --> 00:16:43,488
that everything works correctly and that if

402
00:16:43,552 --> 00:16:46,172
we were to change the code, we can quickly

403
00:16:46,204 --> 00:16:49,049
validate if it still works as intended. So

404
00:16:49,081 --> 00:16:51,299
again, no third-party package involved here,

405
00:16:51,668 --> 00:16:55,253
just some unit tests written and executed

406
00:16:55,349 --> 00:16:56,940
with help of the Bun test runner.
